            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0725" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 165.102/79b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-26">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 26, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>265. Is potash to be used for agricultural and manufacturing purposes and other
                    articles mentioned in recent instructions for American use only in same category
                    with cyanide, dyestuffs, chemicals, and medicines? Have called conference for
                    September 30 looking toward sending American ship to Rotterdam. Have you
                    suggestions for conference?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
